Package: camx-dkms
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 dkms,
Description: Qualcomm CamX - DKMS kernel driver
 Qualcomm CamX is a camera enablement stack for Snapdragon platforms. It
 leverages a number of hardware blocks and software algorithms to
 optimize the streaming of camera data.
 .
 This package provides the DKMS driver which is responsible for:
  * Camera sensor management and configuration
  * Image Signal Processor (ISP/Spectra) pipeline control
  * Camera Request Manager (CRM) for multi-camera synchronization
  * Memory management for camera buffers (ION/DMA)
  * Power management and bandwidth voting for camera subsystems
  * Camera hardware register programming (IFE, BPS, IPE, ICP, JPEG, CCI)
  * Providing V4L2/media controller interface to userspace
  * Sensor communication via I2C/CCI (Camera Control Interface)
  * Flash, actuator, and OIS (Optical Image Stabilization) sub-device control

Package: camx-linux-dev
Architecture: arm64
Provides: camx-uapi-dev
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: Qualcomm CamX - Linux kernel headers (UAPI)
 Qualcomm CamX is a camera enablement stack for Snapdragon platforms. It
 leverages a number of hardware blocks and software algorithms to
 optimize the streaming of camera data.
 .
 This package provides the Linux kernel headers specifically needed to
 build userspace libraries and applications for CamX (UAPI).
